    "author": "Ayesha Rai",
    "date": "6 September 2026",
    "content": "<p>How to use the CEAC portal and other official tools to track your visa application after the interview. Knowing where to look saves stress and helps you avoid unofficial websites that charge for free information.</p><h2>Using CEAC</h2><p>Keep your DS-160 barcode number and interview location handy. Enter them at the official CEAC website to see statuses like Administrative Processing, Issued, or Refused.</p><h2>What the status means</h2><p>Issued means your visa is approved and being printed. Administrative Processing means additional review is needed, which can take days or weeks. Refused may be temporary or permanent depending on the code.</p>"
