    "author": "Ayesha Rai",
    "date": "7 September 2026",
    "content": "<p>What to look for in a hospital, from specialist availability and emergency care to insurance acceptance and patient reviews. Choosing the right facility can make a real difference in both cost and outcomes.</p><h2>Key factors</h2><ul><li><strong>Specialties.</strong> Make sure the hospital has experience with your condition.</li><li><strong>Emergency access.</strong> Distance and response time matter in urgent situations.</li><li><strong>Insurance network.</strong> Out-of-network care can be far more expensive.</li></ul><h2>Questions to ask</h2><p>Ask about infection rates, read patient reviews, and check accreditation. A short phone call to the billing department can also reveal hidden costs.</p>"
