    "date": "8 September 2026",
    "content": "<p>A simple guide to reading hospital charges, insurance Explanation of Benefits, and how to dispute unexpected fees. Medical bills can be confusing, but they are not impossible to understand.</p><h2>Read the itemised bill</h2><p>Ask for an itemised statement. Look for duplicate charges, incorrect dates, or services you did not receive. Compare each line to your insurance Explanation of Benefits.</p><h2>When something looks wrong</h2><p>Call the hospital billing office first. Many errors are fixed quickly. If the dispute continues, ask for a patient advocate or file a formal appeal with your insurer.</p>"
