    "author": "Ayesha Rai",
    "date": "9 September 2026",
    "content": "<p>A practical checklist of documents, clothing, toiletries, and comfort items for a smoother admission and recovery. A little preparation reduces stress for both you and your family.</p><h2>Documents</h2><p>Bring your ID, insurance card, list of medications, and any advance directives. Keep copies in a folder that stays with you.</p><h2>Personal items</h2><p>Pack loose comfortable clothes, slippers with grip, basic toiletries, a phone charger, and earplugs. Leave valuables at home.</p><h2>For recovery</h2><p>Add a notebook to track symptoms and questions, plus a small bag for discharge day when you are ready to go home.</p>"
