    "author": "Ayesha Rai",
    "date": "10 September 2026",
    "content": "<p>When to go to the ER, when urgent care is enough, and how to decide quickly when someone is unwell. Making the right choice can save money and, in serious cases, save a life.</p><h2>Go to the ER for</h2><ul><li>Chest pain, difficulty breathing, severe bleeding, signs of stroke, head injury, or major trauma.</li></ul><h2>Use urgent care for</h2><ul><li>Minor cuts, sprains, ear infections, sore throats, and mild fever.</li></ul><h2>When unsure</h2><p>If you are not certain, call your local nurse hotline or emergency number for guidance. It is better to ask than to delay critical care.</p>"
