    "date": "11 September 2026",
    "content": "<p>Evidence-based tips for post-surgery recovery, from movement and nutrition to wound care and follow-up visits. Recovery is a process you can influence with small daily choices.</p><h2>Move early</h2><p>Follow your surgeon advice on walking and gentle activity. Early movement reduces complications like blood clots and speeds healing.</p><h2>Eat and hydrate</h2><p>Protein, fluids, and fibre support tissue repair and prevent constipation from pain medication. Avoid alcohol until your doctor clears it.</p><h2>Watch for warning signs</h2><p>Fever, increasing pain, redness, swelling, or wound drainage can signal infection. Contact your care team immediately if these appear.</p>"
